{"page": 5, "page_size": 50, "total_matching": 248578, "total_pages": 4972, "cards_html": "\n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248378 · SUBLANGENG_Q495794</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_8CE92755D90A (Question 1 of 1)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high17984)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_8CE92755D90A · Question 1 of 1</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>New research at Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis shows that people who struggle with mood problems or addiction can safely quit smoking and that kicking the habit is associated with improved mental health.</p><p>Cavazos-Rehg, an assistant professor of psychiatry, found that quitting or significantly cutting back on cigarette smoking was linked to improved mental health outcomes. Quitting altogether or reducing by half the number of cigarettes smoked daily was associated with lower risk for mood disorders like depression, as well as a lower likelihood of alcohol and drug problems.</p><p>&quot;We don&#x27;t know if their mental health improves first and then they are more motivated to quit smoking or if quitting smoking leads to an improvement in mental health,&quot; Cavazos-Rehg said. &quot;But either way, our findings show a strong link between quitting and a better psychiatric outlook.&quot;</p><p>In addition, she believes the serious health risks associated with smoking make it important for doctors to work with their patients to quit, regardless of other psychiatric problems.</p><p>&quot;About half of all smokers die from related to smoking, so we need to remember that as complicated as it can be to treat mental health issues, smoking cigarettes also causes very serious illnesses that can lead to death,&quot; she explained.</p><p>Cavazos-Rehg and her team analyzed questionnaires gathered as part of the National Epidemiologic Study on Alcohol and Related Conditions. In the early 2000s, just under 35,000 people were surveyed. As part of the study, they answered questions about drinking, smoking and mental health in two interviews conducted three years apart.</p><p>The researchers focused on data from 4,800 daily smokers. Those who had addiction or other psychiatric problems at the time of the first survey were less likely to have those same problems three years later if they had quit smoking. And those who hadn&#x27;t had psychiatric problems at the initial survey were less likely to develop those problems later if they already had quit.</p><p>&quot;We really need to spread the word and encourage doctors and patients to tackle these problems,&quot; Cavazos-Rehg said. &quot;When a patient is ready to focus on other mental health issues, it may be an ideal time to address smoking cessation, too.&quot;</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>What is the main idea of the passage?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Smoking was associated with alcohol and drug problems.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Quitting smoking may help to improve mental health.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Smoking can lead to cancer or other deadly problems.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Those who had mental problem are more motivated to quit smoking.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The central finding is that quitting smoking or reducing cigarette consumption is associated with improved mental health. The passage specifically reports lower risks of mood disorders, including depression, and reduced likelihood of alcohol and drug problems among those who quit or substantially cut back. Therefore, option B accurately captures the main idea. Option A presents only a supporting detail, while C introduces an unrelated health consequence and D asserts an unsupported motivation for quitting.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high17984) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>d9f9b944b0031ee27144...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248377 · SUBLANGENG_Q495780</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_6A7F5B36BD57 (Question 1 of 1)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high15438)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_6A7F5B36BD57 · Question 1 of 1</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>&quot;What is the most important thing you&#x27;ve done in your life?&quot; The question was put to me during a presentation I gave to a group of lawyers.</p><p>The answer came to me in an instant. It&#x27;s not the one I gave, because the situation was not right. As a lawyer in the entertainment industry, I knew the audience wanted to hear some amusing stories about my work with well-known people, but here&#x27;s the true answer:</p><p>The most important thing I&#x27;ve ever done occurred on October 8,1990. I began the day playing tennis with an old friend I hadn&#x27;t seen for a while. Between points we talked about what had been happening in each other&#x27;s lives. He and his wife had just had a baby boy, who was keeping them up at night.</p><p>While we were playing, a car came screaming up the road toward the courts. It was my friend&#x27;s father, who shouted to my friend that his baby had stopped breathing and was being rushed to the hospital. In a flash my friend was in the car and gone, disappearing in a cloud of dust.</p><p>For a moment I just stood there, paralyzed . Then I tried to figure out what I should do. Follow my friend to the hospital? There was nothing I could accomplish there, I convinced myself. My friend&#x27;s son was in the care of doctors and nurses, and nothing I could do or say would affect the outcome. Be there for moral support? Well, maybe. But my friend and his wife both had large families, and I knew they&#x27;d be surrounded by relatives who would provide more than enough comfort and support, whatever happened. All I could do at the hospital, I decided, was to get in the way. Also, I had planned a full day with my family, who were waiting for me to get home. So I decided to head back to my house and check in my friend later.</p><p>As I started my car, I realized that my friend had left his truck and keys at the courts. I now faced another problem. I couldn&#x27;t leave the keys in the truck. So I decided to go to the hospital and give him the keys.</p><p>When I arrived, I was directed to a room where my friend and his wife were waiting. As I had thought, the room was filled with family members silently watching my friend comfort his wife. I went in and stood by the door, trying to decide what to do next. Soon a doctor appeared. He approached my friend and his wife, and in a quiet voice told them that their son had died.</p><p>For a long time the two held each other and cried, unaware of the rest of us standing around in pained silence. After they had calmed themselves, the doctor suggested they spend a few moments with their son.</p><p>My friend and his wife stood up and walked past their families. When they reached the door, my friend saw me standing in the corner. He came over and hugged me and started to cry. My friend&#x27;s wife hugged me, too, and said , &quot;Thanks for being here.&quot;</p><p>For the rest of that morning, I sat in the emergency room of that hospital and watched my friend and his wife hold the body of their infant son, and say goodbye.</p><p>It&#x27;s the most important thing I have ever done. The experience taught me two lessons.</p><p>First: The most important thing I&#x27;ve ever done happened when I was completely helpless. None of the things I had learned in university, in three years of law school or in six years of legal practice were of any use in that situation. Something terrible was happening to people I cared about, and I was powerless to change the outcome. All I could do was standing by and watching it happen. And yet it was critical that I do just that--- just be there when someone needed me.</p><p>Second: The most important thing I&#x27;ve done almost didn&#x27;t happen because of things I had learned in classroom and professional life. Law school taught me how to take a set of facts, break them down and organized them. These skills are critical for lawyers. When people come to us for help, they&#x27;re often stressed out and depend on a lawyer to think logically. But while learning to think, I almost forget how to feel. Today I have no doubt that I should have leapt into my car without hesitation and followed my friend to the hospital.</p><p>From that one experience I learned that the most important thing in life isn&#x27;t the money you make, the status you attain or the honors you achieve.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>When he was asked about the most important thing he had done in life at a presentation, the author    _   .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">felt it was not an interesting question</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">thought for a while and spoke his mind</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">gave an answer from a lawyer&#x27;s point of view</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">didn&#x27;t give the real answer</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explicitly states that the answer came to the author's mind instantly, but he did not give it because the situation was inappropriate. As a lawyer in the entertainment industry, he understood that his audience expected amusing professional anecdotes involving famous personalities. Therefore, he deliberately withheld his genuine answer and gave a different response. Option D is correct. Option B is incorrect because he did not speak his mind, while A and C lack textual support.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high15438) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:gpt-4o-mini)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>5e7edfec1d51e78b63a7...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248376 · SUBLANGENG_Q495779</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_74E5E44C88CD (Question 5 of 5)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high18377)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_74E5E44C88CD · Question 5 of 5</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A new law helps people with disabilities. The law says that people with disabilities must be able to get into and out of all public buildings. It also says that business must offer special services to people who have special needs. Companies can not refuse to hire disabled workers. Many businesses may have to change their buildings and services.</p><p>--Ramps must be built so people can get into buildings.</p><p>--Movie theatres must have space for people in wheelchairs and seats for their friends to sit near them.</p><p>--Elevators must have floor number in  _ .</p><p>This law will help millions of people. One woman who has been in a wheelchair for many years said, &quot;It is like a dream.&quot;</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The fact that the new law has been passed shows that  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the government has paid no attention to the disabilities</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the government wants to help these disabilities</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">normal people show mercy to the disabilities</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">companies will hire millions of disabled people</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explicitly states that the new law requires public buildings to be accessible, businesses to provide special services and companies not to refuse employment to disabled workers. These legal requirements demonstrate the government's intention to protect and support people with disabilities. Therefore, option B is correct. Option A directly contradicts the passage, option C incorrectly attributes the law to public sympathy, and option D makes an unsupported claim about millions of actual hires.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high18377) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>093cf745ac5b55581f7e...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248375 · SUBLANGENG_Q495778</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_74E5E44C88CD (Question 4 of 5)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high18377)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_74E5E44C88CD · Question 4 of 5</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A new law helps people with disabilities. The law says that people with disabilities must be able to get into and out of all public buildings. It also says that business must offer special services to people who have special needs. Companies can not refuse to hire disabled workers. Many businesses may have to change their buildings and services.</p><p>--Ramps must be built so people can get into buildings.</p><p>--Movie theatres must have space for people in wheelchairs and seats for their friends to sit near them.</p><p>--Elevators must have floor number in  _ .</p><p>This law will help millions of people. One woman who has been in a wheelchair for many years said, &quot;It is like a dream.&quot;</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>What do you think the disabled would feel about the new law?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">They may think the new law reasonable.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Some of them are sure to be for the new law.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">They must feel very excited and happy.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">They feel it is like a dream.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explains that the law improves accessibility through ramps, wheelchair-friendly cinema seating, Braille elevator indicators and equal employment opportunities. These provisions support the inference that people with disabilities would generally consider the law reasonable and beneficial. Option A is the most defensible answer because it expresses a cautious inference. Options C and D assume emotional reactions unsupported by the passage, while B makes an unnecessarily limited claim about support.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high18377) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>ba24cf66643ada96b014...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248374 · SUBLANGENG_Q495777</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_74E5E44C88CD (Question 3 of 5)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high18377)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_74E5E44C88CD · Question 3 of 5</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A new law helps people with disabilities. The law says that people with disabilities must be able to get into and out of all public buildings. It also says that business must offer special services to people who have special needs. Companies can not refuse to hire disabled workers. Many businesses may have to change their buildings and services.</p><p>--Ramps must be built so people can get into buildings.</p><p>--Movie theatres must have space for people in wheelchairs and seats for their friends to sit near them.</p><p>--Elevators must have floor number in  _ .</p><p>This law will help millions of people. One woman who has been in a wheelchair for many years said, &quot;It is like a dream.&quot;</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The word &quot;Braille&quot; means_.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">words known by foreigners</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">words known by common people</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">words on walls</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">words known by the blind</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Braille is a tactile writing and reading system consisting of raised dots that enable people who are blind or visually impaired to read using their fingertips. In the passage, the reference to elevator floor numbers in Braille indicates an accessibility measure for visually impaired individuals. Option D is therefore the intended answer. Options A and B incorrectly describe ordinary vocabulary, while C confuses the location or appearance of information with the specific reading system.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high18377) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>e0f24d9bbf115a0a9a2c...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248373 · SUBLANGENG_Q495776</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_74E5E44C88CD (Question 2 of 5)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high18377)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_74E5E44C88CD · Question 2 of 5</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A new law helps people with disabilities. The law says that people with disabilities must be able to get into and out of all public buildings. It also says that business must offer special services to people who have special needs. Companies can not refuse to hire disabled workers. Many businesses may have to change their buildings and services.</p><p>--Ramps must be built so people can get into buildings.</p><p>--Movie theatres must have space for people in wheelchairs and seats for their friends to sit near them.</p><p>--Elevators must have floor number in  _ .</p><p>This law will help millions of people. One woman who has been in a wheelchair for many years said, &quot;It is like a dream.&quot;</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Ramps can help people_.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">with hearing problems</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">who have difficulty in using their hands</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">who have difficulty in using their legs or feet</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">who don&#x27;t like stairs</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Ramps provide an alternative to stairs and make entrances accessible to people with mobility impairments. Individuals who have difficulty walking or using their legs or feet, including wheelchair users, can use ramps to enter buildings more easily. Therefore, option C is correct. Hearing difficulties concern auditory accessibility, while hand-related difficulties are not the primary issue addressed by ramps. Option D is too general because ramps serve accessibility needs rather than mere dislike of stairs.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high18377) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:gpt-4o-mini)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>f9ea6bdc94fbd7e1b224...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248372 · SUBLANGENG_Q495775</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_74E5E44C88CD (Question 1 of 5)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high18377)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_74E5E44C88CD · Question 1 of 5</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A new law helps people with disabilities. The law says that people with disabilities must be able to get into and out of all public buildings. It also says that business must offer special services to people who have special needs. Companies can not refuse to hire disabled workers. Many businesses may have to change their buildings and services.</p><p>--Ramps must be built so people can get into buildings.</p><p>--Movie theatres must have space for people in wheelchairs and seats for their friends to sit near them.</p><p>--Elevators must have floor number in  _ .</p><p>This law will help millions of people. One woman who has been in a wheelchair for many years said, &quot;It is like a dream.&quot;</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>According to the passage we can see that_.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">it will be difficult for the normal persons to get into the public buildings</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the buildings of all the businesses will have to be changed</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Most businesses used to offer special services to people who have special needs</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">it was difficult for the disabled workers to find jobs in the past</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage states that the new law prohibits companies from refusing to hire workers with disabilities. This provision implies that disabled applicants previously faced employment discrimination, making it difficult for them to obtain jobs. Therefore, option D is the most reasonable inference. Option A contradicts the accessibility objective, B incorrectly suggests every business must change its buildings, and C makes an unsupported claim about widespread previous special services.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high18377) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:gpt-4o-mini)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>a86ae8566c1e17a4e9fa...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248371 · SUBLANGENG_Q495774</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_1043FCE32E5E (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high8556)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_1043FCE32E5E · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>One of the traditions which is now a necessary part of Christmas is a that of Father Christmas, or Santa Claus. According to the modern legend, he is a magical figure who visits all the children of the world during the night before Christmas Day, leaving presents which they find the next morning. He flies through the night sky in a sledge pulled by reindeer, and enters houses by climbing down chimneys. This strange legend is based on the life of a man called Nicholas, but in fact we know very little about him. Historians think he was a Christian bishop in Turkey in about 285--350 A.D. One of the stories about him is that he helped three poor girls. No one would marry them because they were so poor. To provide them with money for their weddings, Nicholas secretly dropped some gold coins down the chimney of their house. After Nicholas died, he was made a saint  by the church.(The name Santa Claus thus comes from St Nicholas.) His feast day was celebrated in December, and parents started giving their children secret presents from St Nicholas. Over the years, this custom became part of our Christmas traditions.</p><p>Recently, a psychologist has claimed that Father Christmas is &quot;the perfect fantasy&quot; for children. According to Professor Anthony Clare, children love the character of Father Christmas because he is like an ideal father: he loves children and gives them presents, but he never criticizes them, is never angry, and children do not even need to thank him for the presents. Other writers, however, point out that Father Christmas can be a frightening character to some children. Jane Bidder says that some children are terrified of this fat, bearded old man. It can certainly confuse many children. As parents, we warn our children to be careful of strangers and never to let them into the house, and yet we tell children that a strange man will come into their bedroom at night! Some children can become very worried about this idea and fear that he is a kind of burglar.</p><p>Most children, however, understand from their parents and from the media that Father Christmas is basically a _ character, and look forward to his annual visit with joy and excitement.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The best title for this passage would be  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Is Father Christmas Dangerous?</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The True History of St Nicholas</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The Legend of Santa Claus</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The Traditions of Christmas</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The best title should reflect the central theme rather than a minor detail. The passage primarily describes the modern legend of Santa Claus, including his Christmas Eve visits, reindeer-drawn sledge, chimney entry and historical connection with St Nicholas. Option C, 'The Legend of Santa Claus', accurately captures this overall subject. Option B focuses too narrowly on historical facts, while A introduces an unsupported danger and D concerns Christmas traditions more generally.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high8556) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:gpt-4o-mini)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>72af592c5d94c0845fd5...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248370 · SUBLANGENG_Q495772</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_1043FCE32E5E (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high8556)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_1043FCE32E5E · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>One of the traditions which is now a necessary part of Christmas is a that of Father Christmas, or Santa Claus. According to the modern legend, he is a magical figure who visits all the children of the world during the night before Christmas Day, leaving presents which they find the next morning. He flies through the night sky in a sledge pulled by reindeer, and enters houses by climbing down chimneys. This strange legend is based on the life of a man called Nicholas, but in fact we know very little about him. Historians think he was a Christian bishop in Turkey in about 285--350 A.D. One of the stories about him is that he helped three poor girls. No one would marry them because they were so poor. To provide them with money for their weddings, Nicholas secretly dropped some gold coins down the chimney of their house. After Nicholas died, he was made a saint  by the church.(The name Santa Claus thus comes from St Nicholas.) His feast day was celebrated in December, and parents started giving their children secret presents from St Nicholas. Over the years, this custom became part of our Christmas traditions.</p><p>Recently, a psychologist has claimed that Father Christmas is &quot;the perfect fantasy&quot; for children. According to Professor Anthony Clare, children love the character of Father Christmas because he is like an ideal father: he loves children and gives them presents, but he never criticizes them, is never angry, and children do not even need to thank him for the presents. Other writers, however, point out that Father Christmas can be a frightening character to some children. Jane Bidder says that some children are terrified of this fat, bearded old man. It can certainly confuse many children. As parents, we warn our children to be careful of strangers and never to let them into the house, and yet we tell children that a strange man will come into their bedroom at night! Some children can become very worried about this idea and fear that he is a kind of burglar.</p><p>Most children, however, understand from their parents and from the media that Father Christmas is basically a _ character, and look forward to his annual visit with joy and excitement.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The writer mentions details such as Father Christmas&#x27;s sledge, the reindeer and the way he climbs down chimneys because he/she  _</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">wants to make it clear that these things are impossible</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">is describing the history of St Nicholas</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">wants everyone to believe that Father Christmas is real</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">is explaining the modern legend of Father Christmas</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The correct answer is <strong>Option D</strong>. The opening sentences explicitly introduce Father Christmas as a figure from modern Christmas tradition and describe his legendary activities. The sledge, reindeer and chimney details illustrate the characteristics of this popular legend. Option A incorrectly assumes that the writer's purpose is to disprove these details, while B confuses the modern legend with the historical account of St Nicholas. Option C incorrectly suggests that the writer intends to establish the figure's literal existence.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high8556) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>9221521ad11f6ff11de7...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248369 · SUBLANGENG_Q495770</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_2059920280A2 (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high11886)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_2059920280A2 · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>The first time Luca heard the Island of Inventions, he was very young, but the wonders he heard about sounded so unbelievable to him that they were forever kept in his memory. Since then, he never stopped searching clues which might lead him to that place of wonder. He read widely to collect information.</p><p>Taking a little from here and there, he got quite a clear idea of what the Island was really like. It was a secret place, where all the great men learn and invent together. To be able to join that select club, you had to have created great inventions. Only then could you receive the invitation.</p><p>To get a chance, Luca spend the years studying and inventing. Every new idea he got, he made it into an invention, and if there were anything he didn&#x27;t understand, he would seek help. Soon he met other brilliant inventors too, and he told them of the secrets of the Island. These young inventors would likewise dream of being sent &quot;the letter&quot;.</p><p>As time passed, the disappointment of not being sent the letter gave rise to even greater cooperation and help between them. Their inventions soon became known throughout the world.</p><p>But no invention came.</p><p>They didn&#x27;t lose heart. They continued learning and inventing, trying to come up with better ideas. Fresh talent was added to their group. One day, Luca, already very old, was speaking with a brilliant young man who had written to join their group. Luca told the young man the secrets of the Island, and of how he was sure that they would receive an invitation. Surprised, the young inventor said: &quot;What? You mean this isn&#x27;t really the Island of Inventions?&quot;</p><p>It inspired Luca and he realized that his dream had become true.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Luca and other brilliant inventors around him shared a dream of   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">being great inventors of worldwide fame</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">being accepted as members of the Island of Inventions</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">being inventors envied by members of the Island of Inventions</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">being remembered for the contribution to scientific development</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The text explains that the Island of Inventions is a secret, select club where great inventors learn and collaborate, and one must create great inventions to receive an invitation to join. Therefore, Luca and other brilliant inventors shared the dream of being accepted as members of this prestigious island. Option A focuses on fame rather than membership, Option C suggests envy which is not the primary shared dream, and Option D is too broad and not the specific goal of joining the island.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high11886) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>8bbe3db4d101ae46de2c...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248368 · SUBLANGENG_Q495769</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_2059920280A2 (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high11886)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_2059920280A2 · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>The first time Luca heard the Island of Inventions, he was very young, but the wonders he heard about sounded so unbelievable to him that they were forever kept in his memory. Since then, he never stopped searching clues which might lead him to that place of wonder. He read widely to collect information.</p><p>Taking a little from here and there, he got quite a clear idea of what the Island was really like. It was a secret place, where all the great men learn and invent together. To be able to join that select club, you had to have created great inventions. Only then could you receive the invitation.</p><p>To get a chance, Luca spend the years studying and inventing. Every new idea he got, he made it into an invention, and if there were anything he didn&#x27;t understand, he would seek help. Soon he met other brilliant inventors too, and he told them of the secrets of the Island. These young inventors would likewise dream of being sent &quot;the letter&quot;.</p><p>As time passed, the disappointment of not being sent the letter gave rise to even greater cooperation and help between them. Their inventions soon became known throughout the world.</p><p>But no invention came.</p><p>They didn&#x27;t lose heart. They continued learning and inventing, trying to come up with better ideas. Fresh talent was added to their group. One day, Luca, already very old, was speaking with a brilliant young man who had written to join their group. Luca told the young man the secrets of the Island, and of how he was sure that they would receive an invitation. Surprised, the young inventor said: &quot;What? You mean this isn&#x27;t really the Island of Inventions?&quot;</p><p>It inspired Luca and he realized that his dream had become true.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Luca read widely to   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">get information about the great inventions</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">get clear ideas about the island for vacations</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">seek massages about the secret club of inventions</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">get more knowledge for the benefit of his inventions</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage states that Luca wanted to find clues leading to the Island of Inventions, a secret club of great inventors, and therefore read widely to collect information about it. This directly aligns with seeking messages or information about this secret club of inventions. Option A is too narrow, Option B misinterprets the island as a vacation destination, and Option D is not the primary motive described in the text.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high11886) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>3efd89f8c679c538b231...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248367 · SUBLANGENG_Q495768</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_54F7ACDF56AB (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high19192)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_54F7ACDF56AB · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A rare butterfly has been discovered in Britain for the first time in 60 years,having moved from Eastern Europe.The only previous record of a wild yellow-legged Tortoiseshell in Britain was in 1953,when it was seen just once in Sevenoaks,Kent.Several weeks ago,there were already four confirmed sightings,along the East coast in Norfolk,Suffolk and Kent,and six further reports of the butterfly in coastal areas. Conservationists are very excited about the    sightings,which are rare in the butterfly world.</p><p>The butterflies are thought to have flown on easterly winds across Europe in the last few weeks.The large and colourful insect mainly lives in Eastern Europe.In recent years,it has spread into Scandinavia and its number increases rapidly during warm weather.Also known as the Scarce Tortoiseshell,it has an orange and blue colour and is about one third bigger than our own Small Tortoiseshell.</p><p>Butterfly Conservation was starting its annual Big Butterfly Count,a yearly survey of the butterflies across the nation.Sir David Attenborough,President of the charity,said,&quot;The UK is a nation of amateur naturalists and we have a proud tradition of celebrating and studying our wildlife.By taking part in the Big Butterfly Count this summer,you can contribute to discovering the fantastic butterflies and other wildlife that share your garden,parks and    countryside.&quot;He added,&quot;Butterflies fought back last year after a terrible 2012 but despite this,butterfly numbers were still below average.Three quarters of the UK&#x27;s butterflies are in decline and one third are in danger of dying out.This is bad news for the UK&#x27;s birds,bees,bats and other wildlife.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>What&#x27;s the main idea of the text?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Butterflies are quite rare in Britain.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Butterflies like travelling frequently.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">A rare butterfly appeared in Britain.</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The butterfly world changed a lot.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage describes the rare sighting of the yellow-legged Tortoiseshell butterfly in Britain for the first time in sixty years, highlighting multiple recent sightings along the east coast. Thus, the main idea is that a rare butterfly has appeared in Britain. Option A is too general, Option B is incorrect as they do not travel for leisure, and Option D is unsupported by the text.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high19192) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>4c352b5dad4e5b8870d5...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248366 · SUBLANGENG_Q495766</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_54F7ACDF56AB (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high19192)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_54F7ACDF56AB · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A rare butterfly has been discovered in Britain for the first time in 60 years,having moved from Eastern Europe.The only previous record of a wild yellow-legged Tortoiseshell in Britain was in 1953,when it was seen just once in Sevenoaks,Kent.Several weeks ago,there were already four confirmed sightings,along the East coast in Norfolk,Suffolk and Kent,and six further reports of the butterfly in coastal areas. Conservationists are very excited about the    sightings,which are rare in the butterfly world.</p><p>The butterflies are thought to have flown on easterly winds across Europe in the last few weeks.The large and colourful insect mainly lives in Eastern Europe.In recent years,it has spread into Scandinavia and its number increases rapidly during warm weather.Also known as the Scarce Tortoiseshell,it has an orange and blue colour and is about one third bigger than our own Small Tortoiseshell.</p><p>Butterfly Conservation was starting its annual Big Butterfly Count,a yearly survey of the butterflies across the nation.Sir David Attenborough,President of the charity,said,&quot;The UK is a nation of amateur naturalists and we have a proud tradition of celebrating and studying our wildlife.By taking part in the Big Butterfly Count this summer,you can contribute to discovering the fantastic butterflies and other wildlife that share your garden,parks and    countryside.&quot;He added,&quot;Butterflies fought back last year after a terrible 2012 but despite this,butterfly numbers were still below average.Three quarters of the UK&#x27;s butterflies are in decline and one third are in danger of dying out.This is bad news for the UK&#x27;s birds,bees,bats and other wildlife.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>These rare butterflies usually live in  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Eastern Europe</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Norfolk,Suffolk and Kent</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">coastal areas</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Sevenoaks,Kent</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage identifies Eastern Europe as the butterfly's place of origin, explaining that it recently moved to Britain on easterly winds across Europe. Norfolk, Suffolk, Kent, and Sevenoaks are locations of reported British sightings, not its usual habitat. Therefore, Eastern Europe is the best-supported answer. Options B, C, and D confuse temporary sighting locations in Britain with the species' usual geographical distribution.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high19192) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:gpt-4o-mini)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>ac357234ce53246544f0...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248365 · SUBLANGENG_Q495765</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_9EACAC0AB3B9 (Question 1 of 1)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high10134)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_9EACAC0AB3B9 · Question 1 of 1</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Hi, everybody!</p><p>Welcome to our newly-opened Richards Cinema Bookstore!</p><p>Now let me introduce to you some of the new film books in our store.</p><p>Are you Chinese film fans? OK, here comes the latest 25 New Takes about Chinese films. It is a collection of 25 fresh readings of different Chinese films from the 1930s to the present. In recent years, Chinese films are very popular in the States, such as Crouching Tiger and Hidden Dragon, Hero, and Flowers of Shanghai.</p><p>Do you like French films? Well, here is The French Cinema Book. It covers French films from the 1890s to the beginning of the 21st century. It is written for all lovers of French cinema: students and teachers, specialists and fans, and so on.</p><p>Maybe you are Indian film fans and star-chasers. Then here is Encyclopedia  of Indian Cinema. The book is complete introduction to all the best Indian films. It also offers a full list of names of the famous and successful film stars in the past ten years. You know, the Indian film industry is the largest in the world after our Hollywood.</p><p>If you like British films, we have The British Cinema Book. It is a good review of British cinema. This book contains a good many nice pictures.</p><p>In our bookstore, you can also find books about Mexican, Japanese, Australian, German and Italian films.</p><p>Well, please help yourselves to some coffee or tea, and have a good time here!</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The purpose of the speaker is   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">to satisfy the customers&#x27; various tastes</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">to keep the authors in the cinema bookstore</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">to offer the tourists chances to meet the film stars</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">to turn the readers into film producers</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The speaker introduces different books about Chinese and French cinema to appeal to customers with varied interests. The collection <em>25 New Takes</em> targets Chinese film enthusiasts, while <em>The French Cinema Book</em> caters to lovers of French films. These examples demonstrate the bookstore's intention to satisfy diverse customer preferences. Options B, C, and D are unsupported because the passage mentions neither retaining authors, meeting film stars, nor training readers to become film producers.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high10134) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:gpt-4o-mini)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>c6fa2a76c5451416c15a...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248364 · SUBLANGENG_Q495763</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_04C752D6E111 (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high11664)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_04C752D6E111 · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>What does it mean to say that we live in a world of persuasion? It means that we live among competing interests. Your roommate&#x27;s need to study for an exam may take priority   over pizza. Your instructor may have good reasons not to change your grade.</p><p>In such a world, persuasion is the art of getting others to give fair and favorable consideration to our points of view. When we persuade, we want to influence how others believe and behave. We may not always _ -- other points of view may be more persuasive, depending on the listener, the situation, and the merit of the case. But when we practice the art of persuasion, we try to ensure that our position receives the attention it deserves.</p><p>Some people, however, object to the very idea of persuasion. They may regard it as an unwelcome interruption into their lives. Just the opposite, we believe that persuasion is unavoidable -- to live is to persuade. Persuasion may be ethical   or unethical, selfless or selfish, inspiring or degrading. Persuaders may enlighten our minds or get our vulnerability . Ethical persuasion, however, calls on sound reasoning and is sensitive to the feelings and needs of listeners. Such persuasion can help us apply the wisdom of the past to the decisions we now must make. Therefore, the most basic part of education is learning to resist the one kind of persuasion and to encourage and practice the other.</p><p>Beyond its personal importance to us, persuasion is necessary to society. The right to persuade and be persuaded is the bedrock of the American political system, guaranteed by the First Amendment to the Constitution  .</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The passage mainly discusses   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">that people persuade to get what they want</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">that people persuade in different ways</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">that persuasion is widely accepted and appreciated</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">that persuasion is important and it is all around us</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage primarily establishes that persuasion is an essential and widespread feature of everyday life. It opens by describing a world of competing interests, illustrates conflicts involving roommates and instructors, and defines persuasion as obtaining fair and favorable consideration of one's viewpoint. It then explains how persuasion influences beliefs and behavior. Option D captures this central idea, whereas A is too narrow, B emphasizes methods not discussed, and C incorrectly suggests universal acceptance.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high11664) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>0b6c20268b97708a2864...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248363 · SUBLANGENG_Q495761</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_04C752D6E111 (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high11664)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_04C752D6E111 · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>What does it mean to say that we live in a world of persuasion? It means that we live among competing interests. Your roommate&#x27;s need to study for an exam may take priority   over pizza. Your instructor may have good reasons not to change your grade.</p><p>In such a world, persuasion is the art of getting others to give fair and favorable consideration to our points of view. When we persuade, we want to influence how others believe and behave. We may not always _ -- other points of view may be more persuasive, depending on the listener, the situation, and the merit of the case. But when we practice the art of persuasion, we try to ensure that our position receives the attention it deserves.</p><p>Some people, however, object to the very idea of persuasion. They may regard it as an unwelcome interruption into their lives. Just the opposite, we believe that persuasion is unavoidable -- to live is to persuade. Persuasion may be ethical   or unethical, selfless or selfish, inspiring or degrading. Persuaders may enlighten our minds or get our vulnerability . Ethical persuasion, however, calls on sound reasoning and is sensitive to the feelings and needs of listeners. Such persuasion can help us apply the wisdom of the past to the decisions we now must make. Therefore, the most basic part of education is learning to resist the one kind of persuasion and to encourage and practice the other.</p><p>Beyond its personal importance to us, persuasion is necessary to society. The right to persuade and be persuaded is the bedrock of the American political system, guaranteed by the First Amendment to the Constitution  .</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>According to the passage, persuasion means   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">changing others&#x27; points of view</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">exercising power over other people</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">getting other people to consider your point of view</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">getting people to agree with you and do what you want</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explicitly defines persuasion as the art of getting others to give fair and favourable consideration to our points of view. Therefore, option C accurately expresses the author's definition. Persuasion involves influencing beliefs or behaviour, but agreement is not guaranteed. Option A incorrectly suggests that changing viewpoints must occur, B confuses persuasion with exercising power, and D wrongly assumes that successful persuasion always produces agreement and compliance.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high11664) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>44b2e9787eedff8e8671...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248362 · SUBLANGENG_Q495760</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_E810E4602DD7 (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high6885)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_E810E4602DD7 · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>My favourite book is The Adventure of Tom Sawyer by Mark Twain.Tom lives with his aunt Polly in a quiet street of St. Petersburg, Missouri.He&#x27;s a lively and clever young boy,and he finds himself in many exciting adventures.He runs away with his two friends,Huck Finn and Joe,to an island in the middle of the Mississippi River for several days.With Huck he goes looking for treasure, with Becky he gets lost in a cave.and finally,they find a box of gold.</p><p>My favourite scene in the book is when everyone thinks Tom is dead.He decides to go to his own funeral.He hides and watches for a time and then suddenly he appears. Everyone is astonished to see him but they&#x27;re also pleased to see him alive.</p><p>Tom is the hero of the story,but there are other important characters.Huck is an outsider and everyone is afraid of him.Becky is pretty with fair hair,Joe is Tom&#x27;s best friend.and Injun Joe is the bad man of the story.</p><p>The theme of the  story  is about children growing up.It describes how strangers are seen in small towns of America. Finally, it talks about freedom,social rules and how people are  punished for bad behaviour.</p><p>Why do I think The Adventure of Tom Sawyer is a great book? Mark Twain wrote the story in 1876,but it&#x27;s still read and loved by people all over the world today. And although it&#x27;s only a story, Twain wrote it in the everyday English of the southern states of America in  the 19th century,so it sounds very real. Today it&#x27;s thought to be one of the greatest books in American literature. Go on--- read it! I know you&#x27;ll enjoy it,too.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>.The writer writes the article to   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">ask us to read the book</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">tell us how popular the book is today</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">tell us when Mark Twain wrote the story</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">tell us why the story sounds very real</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The writer introduces a favourite book, summarizes its main events, describes memorable adventures, and highlights a favourite scene. This descriptive and appreciative presentation indicates an intention to share enthusiasm for the book and encourage readers to explore it. Thus, option A is the best answer. Option B concerns contemporary popularity, option C asks about publication history, and option D concerns realism; none of these purposes is supported by the passage.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high6885) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>d5c24efca32e64a08e41...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248361 · SUBLANGENG_Q495759</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_E810E4602DD7 (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high6885)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_E810E4602DD7 · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>My favourite book is The Adventure of Tom Sawyer by Mark Twain.Tom lives with his aunt Polly in a quiet street of St. Petersburg, Missouri.He&#x27;s a lively and clever young boy,and he finds himself in many exciting adventures.He runs away with his two friends,Huck Finn and Joe,to an island in the middle of the Mississippi River for several days.With Huck he goes looking for treasure, with Becky he gets lost in a cave.and finally,they find a box of gold.</p><p>My favourite scene in the book is when everyone thinks Tom is dead.He decides to go to his own funeral.He hides and watches for a time and then suddenly he appears. Everyone is astonished to see him but they&#x27;re also pleased to see him alive.</p><p>Tom is the hero of the story,but there are other important characters.Huck is an outsider and everyone is afraid of him.Becky is pretty with fair hair,Joe is Tom&#x27;s best friend.and Injun Joe is the bad man of the story.</p><p>The theme of the  story  is about children growing up.It describes how strangers are seen in small towns of America. Finally, it talks about freedom,social rules and how people are  punished for bad behaviour.</p><p>Why do I think The Adventure of Tom Sawyer is a great book? Mark Twain wrote the story in 1876,but it&#x27;s still read and loved by people all over the world today. And although it&#x27;s only a story, Twain wrote it in the everyday English of the southern states of America in  the 19th century,so it sounds very real. Today it&#x27;s thought to be one of the greatest books in American literature. Go on--- read it! I know you&#x27;ll enjoy it,too.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>.The whole book is mainly about   _   .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">freedom and social rules</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">children&#x27;s bad behaviour</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the growth of young children</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">strangers in American small towns</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage primarily presents Tom Sawyer's childhood experiences, adventures, friendships, and mischievous activities, illustrating aspects of growing up. His adventures with Huck and Joe, his search for treasure, and his experiences with Becky collectively portray the life and development of a young boy. Therefore, option C is the broadest thematic interpretation. Option A is too narrow, B unfairly emphasizes bad behaviour, and D is unrelated to the central theme.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high6885) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>9978e74335f26236cfe8...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248360 · SUBLANGENG_Q495757</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_2B546C4CD09B (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high9374)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_2B546C4CD09B · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Very soon the Rabbit noticed Alice, as she went hunting about, and called out to her, &quot;What are you doing out here? Run home this moment, and fetch me a pair of gloves and a fan! Quick, now!&quot;</p><p>Alice was so much frightened that she ran off at once in the direction it pointed to. She saw a little house, on the door of which was a plate with the name &quot;W. RABBIT&quot;. She went in and hurried upstairs.</p><p>By this time she had found her way into a tidy little room with a table in the window, and on it a fan and two or three pairs of tiny white kid gloves: she took up the fan and a pair of the gloves, and was just going to leave the room, when her eye fell upon a little bottle that stood near the looking-glass. There was no label  this time with the words&#x27; DRINK ME,&#x27; but she opened it and put it to her lips .&quot;I know something interesting is sure to happen,&quot; she said to herself. Before she had drunk half the bottle, she found her head touching the ceiling. She went on growing and very soon had to get down on her knees on the floor. Still she went on growing, and as a last _ , she put one arm out of the window, and one foot up the chimney , and said to herself, &quot;Now I can do no more, whatever happens. What will happen to me?&quot;</p><p>Luckily for Alice, she grew no longer: still it was very uncomfortable, and as there seemed to be no sort of chance of her ever getting out of the room again, no wonder she felt unhappy.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The passage may come from a(an)   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">science book</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">wildlife magazine</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">guide book</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">English novel</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage is a narrative extract featuring fictional characters, dialogue, imaginative events and descriptive storytelling. These are characteristic features of a literary work, particularly a novel. Option D, English novel, is therefore correct. A science book presents scientific information, a wildlife magazine generally discusses animals and nature, and a guidebook provides practical information about places or activities. None of these genres appropriately describes the imaginative narrative presented here.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high9374) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:gpt-4o-mini)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>37e250cc42b6e1c25507...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248359 · SUBLANGENG_Q495755</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_2B546C4CD09B (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high9374)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_2B546C4CD09B · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Very soon the Rabbit noticed Alice, as she went hunting about, and called out to her, &quot;What are you doing out here? Run home this moment, and fetch me a pair of gloves and a fan! Quick, now!&quot;</p><p>Alice was so much frightened that she ran off at once in the direction it pointed to. She saw a little house, on the door of which was a plate with the name &quot;W. RABBIT&quot;. She went in and hurried upstairs.</p><p>By this time she had found her way into a tidy little room with a table in the window, and on it a fan and two or three pairs of tiny white kid gloves: she took up the fan and a pair of the gloves, and was just going to leave the room, when her eye fell upon a little bottle that stood near the looking-glass. There was no label  this time with the words&#x27; DRINK ME,&#x27; but she opened it and put it to her lips .&quot;I know something interesting is sure to happen,&quot; she said to herself. Before she had drunk half the bottle, she found her head touching the ceiling. She went on growing and very soon had to get down on her knees on the floor. Still she went on growing, and as a last _ , she put one arm out of the window, and one foot up the chimney , and said to herself, &quot;Now I can do no more, whatever happens. What will happen to me?&quot;</p><p>Luckily for Alice, she grew no longer: still it was very uncomfortable, and as there seemed to be no sort of chance of her ever getting out of the room again, no wonder she felt unhappy.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>According to the passage, we can know that Alice   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">felt comfortable when she grew no longer</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">was afraid when the Rabbit called out to her</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">knew what would happen to her if she continued to grow</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">saw a label &quot;DRINK ME&quot; on the bottle and drank half of it</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The correct answer is B. The decisive textual evidence is the sentence: \"Alice was so much frightened that she ran off at once.\" The Rabbit's sudden command to fetch gloves and a fan frightened Alice, prompting her immediate obedience. Option A is unsupported because the passage does not establish that she felt comfortable. Options C and D introduce events or details not established in the supplied extract. Therefore, B is the only directly supported answer.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high9374) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>0cc589b576d291adf9dc...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248358 · SUBLANGENG_Q495753</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_EA1627379F4F (Question 1 of 1)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high9049)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_EA1627379F4F · Question 1 of 1</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A couple who held hands at breakfast every morning even after 70 years of marriage have died 15 hours apart. Helen Felumlee, died at 92 on April 12. Her husband, 91-year-old Kenneth Felumlee, died the next morning.</p><p>The couple&#x27;s eight children say the two had been inseparable since meeting as teenagers, once sharing the bottom of a bunk   bed on a ferry rather than sleeping on night apart.</p><p>They remained deeply in love until the very end, even eating breakfast together while holding hands, said their daughter, Linda Cody. &quot;We knew when one went, the other was going to go,&quot; she said. According to Cody, about 12 hours after Helen died, Kenneth looked at his children and said, &quot;Mon&#x27;s dead.&quot; He quickly began to fade, surrounded by 24 of his closest family members and friends when he died the next morning. &quot;He was ready,&quot; Cody said, &quot;He just didn&#x27;t want to leave her here by herself.&quot;</p><p>Son Dick said his parents died of old age, surrounded by family.</p><p>The pair had known each other for several years when they eloped in Newport across the Ohio River from Cincinnati, on Feb. 20, 1994. At two days shy of his 21stbirthday, Kenneth-who went by Kenny-was too young to marry in Ohio. &quot;He couldn&#x27;t wait.&#x27; son Jim said.</p><p>Kenneth worked as a railroad car inspector and mechanic before becoming a mail carrier for the Post Office. He was active in the church as a Sunday teacher.</p><p>Helen stayed at home, not only cooking and cleaning for her own family but also for other families in need in the area. She taught Sunday school, too, but was known more for her greeting card ministry, sending cards for birthdays, sympathy and the holidays to everyone in her community, each with a personal note inside. &quot;She kept Hallmark in business,&quot; daughter-in-law Debbie joked.</p><p>When Kenneth retired in 1983 and the children began to leave the house, the Felumlees began to explore their love of travel, visiting almost all 50 states by bus. &quot;He didn&#x27;t want to fly anywhere because you couldn&#x27;t see anything as you were going,&quot; Jim said.</p><p>Although both experienced declining health in recent years, Cody said, each tried to stay strong for the other. &quot;That&#x27;s what kept them going,&quot; she said.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>From what Cody said, we can learn the children   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">were not in front of their father</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">don&#x27;t look after their father</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">foresaw their father would go</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">surrounded their father</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The correct answer is C. The key evidence is Cody's statement: \"We knew when one went, the other was going to go.\" This indicates that the children anticipated Kenneth's death following Helen's death because of their exceptionally close emotional bond. Therefore, they foresaw that their father would soon die. Options A, B and D concern the children's physical presence or caregiving arrangements, none of which can be inferred from Cody's statement.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high9049) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>b118d6024e6095a98832...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248357 · SUBLANGENG_Q495748</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_60B2DE7E77AA (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high16066)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_60B2DE7E77AA · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A girl with blue eyes is a blue-eyed girl. A man with long legs is a long-legged man. A woman with white hair is a white-haired woman. Children who have good looks are good-looking children. What do you do when you want to buy clothes? You go to a shop. If you can find clothes that are the right size for you, and if they are ready to wear, you will probably buy them. They are called ready-made clothes. If you can not find clothes that are the right size, you will go to a tailor&#x27;s shop. A tailor is a man who makes clothes. He will measure you carefully and will then make clothes for you. Such clothes are called tailor-made clothes.</p><p>What do we call a man who is dressed badly? We call him a badly-dressed man. A woman who is dressed well is called a well-dressed woman.</p><p>What do you wear when it rains heavily? You wear a coat that will keep the rain out. Such a coat is called a raincoat. It is made of waterproof cloth--cloth that does not let water pass through. We have a lot of rain in England. If you come to England, bring a raincoat and an umbrella. You will find them useful.</p><p>If the floor, walls and ceiling of a room are made so that sound cannot pass through the wall, we say that the room is sound-proof. There are sound-proof rooms in all broadcasting stations.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>58. What do you think is the best title for the article?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">The Forms of Compound Words.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Compound Words in Everyday Life</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">How to Use Compound Words.</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Water-proof Cloth in the Best.</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage illustrates compound words and their use in everyday English. Examples include “blue-eyed,” “long-legged,” “white-haired,” “good-looking,” “ready-made,” and “tailor-made.” These expressions combine two elements to form a meaningful word or adjective describing a person or an object. Thus, “Compound Words in Everyday Life” (B) best captures both the examples and their practical context. Option A is narrower, C emphasizes instruction, and D is unrelated to the passage.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high16066) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>d4ca339ad116bfd98533...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248356 · SUBLANGENG_Q495747</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_60B2DE7E77AA (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high16066)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_60B2DE7E77AA · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A girl with blue eyes is a blue-eyed girl. A man with long legs is a long-legged man. A woman with white hair is a white-haired woman. Children who have good looks are good-looking children. What do you do when you want to buy clothes? You go to a shop. If you can find clothes that are the right size for you, and if they are ready to wear, you will probably buy them. They are called ready-made clothes. If you can not find clothes that are the right size, you will go to a tailor&#x27;s shop. A tailor is a man who makes clothes. He will measure you carefully and will then make clothes for you. Such clothes are called tailor-made clothes.</p><p>What do we call a man who is dressed badly? We call him a badly-dressed man. A woman who is dressed well is called a well-dressed woman.</p><p>What do you wear when it rains heavily? You wear a coat that will keep the rain out. Such a coat is called a raincoat. It is made of waterproof cloth--cloth that does not let water pass through. We have a lot of rain in England. If you come to England, bring a raincoat and an umbrella. You will find them useful.</p><p>If the floor, walls and ceiling of a room are made so that sound cannot pass through the wall, we say that the room is sound-proof. There are sound-proof rooms in all broadcasting stations.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>57. On back of a watch we can often see the word &quot;water-proof&quot;. The word means_.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">water won&#x27;t get into the watch</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">you can put water into the watch</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">not putting the watch into water</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">you can see the watch clearly in water</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The adjective “water-proof” means resistant to the penetration of water. In the context of a watch, it indicates that water cannot enter the watch under the conditions for which it is designed to be water-resistant. Therefore, option A expresses the intended meaning. Option B reverses the meaning, option C describes an instruction rather than a property, and option D incorrectly suggests visibility underwater rather than protection against water.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high16066) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>380d0eea37a8326abd37...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248355 · SUBLANGENG_Q495745</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_60B2DE7E77AA (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high16066)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_60B2DE7E77AA · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>A girl with blue eyes is a blue-eyed girl. A man with long legs is a long-legged man. A woman with white hair is a white-haired woman. Children who have good looks are good-looking children. What do you do when you want to buy clothes? You go to a shop. If you can find clothes that are the right size for you, and if they are ready to wear, you will probably buy them. They are called ready-made clothes. If you can not find clothes that are the right size, you will go to a tailor&#x27;s shop. A tailor is a man who makes clothes. He will measure you carefully and will then make clothes for you. Such clothes are called tailor-made clothes.</p><p>What do we call a man who is dressed badly? We call him a badly-dressed man. A woman who is dressed well is called a well-dressed woman.</p><p>What do you wear when it rains heavily? You wear a coat that will keep the rain out. Such a coat is called a raincoat. It is made of waterproof cloth--cloth that does not let water pass through. We have a lot of rain in England. If you come to England, bring a raincoat and an umbrella. You will find them useful.</p><p>If the floor, walls and ceiling of a room are made so that sound cannot pass through the wall, we say that the room is sound-proof. There are sound-proof rooms in all broadcasting stations.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>55. The clothes which you buy from the supermarket are called    _    clothes.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">tailor-made</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">ready-made</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">hand-made</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">mass production</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explicitly defines ready-made clothes as garments that are available in shops, already manufactured, and suitable for immediate wear in standard sizes. Clothes purchased from a supermarket are generally ready-made rather than individually produced for a particular customer's measurements. Therefore, option B is correct. Option A refers to clothes specially made by a tailor, while C describes handmade garments and D refers to a production process rather than the specific clothing category defined in the passage.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high16066) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>f74efde7ddc180a30084...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248354 · SUBLANGENG_Q495744</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_92C2EC1E72E6 (Question 1 of 1)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high2633)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_92C2EC1E72E6 · Question 1 of 1</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>Bungee jumping is an activity about jumping from a tall structure while connected to a large elastic cord . The tall structure is usually a fixed object, such as a building, bridge or crane; but it is also possible to jump from a movable object, such as a hot-air balloon or helicopter, that has the ability to stay over one place on the ground; fixed-wing aircraft are unsuitable because they only stay high when moving quickly forward.</p><p>When the person jumps, the cord stretches to absorb  the energy of the fall, then the jumper flies upwards again as the cord jumps back. The jumper oscillates up and down until all the energy is used up.</p><p>The word bungee first appeared around 1930 and was the name for a rubber eraser. The first modern bungee jumps were made on 1 April 1979 from the 250-foot Clifton Suspension Bridge in Bristol, by David Kirk, Chris Baker and Alan Weston of the Dangerous Sports Club. The jumpers continued with jumps in the US from the Golden Gate and Royal Gorge bridges, spreading the concept worldwide. By 1982 they were jumping from mobile cranes and hot-air balloons. Later they put on commercial shows, which began in 1986.</p><p>As with any sport, injuries can still happen, and there have been deaths. A relatively common mistake in the cases that may cause death is to use a cord that is too long. The cord should be fully shorter than the height of the jumping place to allow it room to jumper either starts to slow down or keeps speeding up depending upon the speed of falling.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The purpose of writing this passage is to  _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">teach people how to carry out a bungee jumping</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">remind people of the danger of bungee jumping</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">advise people not to take the risk of bungee jumping</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">introduce some knowledge about bungee jumping</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage primarily provides general information about bungee jumping, explaining the structures used, the function of the elastic cord, and the jumper's oscillating motion. It describes how the cord absorbs the energy of the fall and subsequently returns the jumper upwards. Therefore, option D correctly identifies the informative purpose. Options A, B, and C are incorrect because the passage neither gives practical instructions nor emphasizes danger or advises against participation.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high2633) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>2903ae27fb82243740a8...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248353 · SUBLANGENG_Q495734</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_A7108733196F (Question 2 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high6268)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_A7108733196F · Question 2 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>There is probably no field of human activity in which our values and lifestyles are shown more clearly and strongly than they are in the clothes that we choose to wear.The dress of an individual is a kind of &quot;sign language&quot; that communicates a set of information and is usually the basis on which immediate impressions are formed.Traditionally,a concern for clothes was considered to be an affair of females,while men took pride in the fact that they were completely lacking in clothes consciousness .</p><p>This type of American culture is by degrees changing as man dress takes on greater variety and color.Even as early as 1955,a researcher in Michigan said that _ White collar workers in particular viewed dress as a symbol of ability,which could be used to impress or influence others,especially in the work situation.The white collar worker was described as extremely concerned about the impression his clothing made on his superiors .Although blue collar workers were less aware that they might be judged on the basis of their clothing,they recognized that any difference from the accepted pattern of dress would be made fun of by fellow workers.</p><p>Since that time,of course,the patterns have changed:the typical office worker may now be wearing the blue shirt,and the laborer a white shirt;but the importance of dress has not become less.Other researchers in recent years have helped to prove its importance in the lives of individuals at various age levels and in different social and economic status groups .</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Traditionally,people usually thought that   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">men cared very much for clothes</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">women were concerned greatly about what they wore while men didn&#x27;t</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">both men and women paid great attention to their clothes</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">neither men nor women showed interest in clothes</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage states that traditionally, concern for clothes was considered an affair of females, whereas men took pride in being completely lacking in clothes consciousness. This contrast establishes that women were traditionally regarded as more concerned about their appearance and clothing than men. Thus, option B accurately represents the author's statement. Option A reverses the gender distinction, while C incorrectly suggests equal concern. Option D is also incorrect because the passage explicitly identifies women's concern about clothing.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high6268) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:gpt-4o-mini)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>1055993073006e3f66b9...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248352 · SUBLANGENG_Q495733</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_A7108733196F (Question 1 of 2)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high6268)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_A7108733196F · Question 1 of 2</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>There is probably no field of human activity in which our values and lifestyles are shown more clearly and strongly than they are in the clothes that we choose to wear.The dress of an individual is a kind of &quot;sign language&quot; that communicates a set of information and is usually the basis on which immediate impressions are formed.Traditionally,a concern for clothes was considered to be an affair of females,while men took pride in the fact that they were completely lacking in clothes consciousness .</p><p>This type of American culture is by degrees changing as man dress takes on greater variety and color.Even as early as 1955,a researcher in Michigan said that _ White collar workers in particular viewed dress as a symbol of ability,which could be used to impress or influence others,especially in the work situation.The white collar worker was described as extremely concerned about the impression his clothing made on his superiors .Although blue collar workers were less aware that they might be judged on the basis of their clothing,they recognized that any difference from the accepted pattern of dress would be made fun of by fellow workers.</p><p>Since that time,of course,the patterns have changed:the typical office worker may now be wearing the blue shirt,and the laborer a white shirt;but the importance of dress has not become less.Other researchers in recent years have helped to prove its importance in the lives of individuals at various age levels and in different social and economic status groups .</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>The passage tells us that   _  .</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">our values and lifestyles are in no field of human activity</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the clothes that we choose to wear have something to do with our values and lifestyles</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">our values and lifestyles are from the sign language</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">the clothes we choose to wear depend on a set of information and immediate impression</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The opening sentence explicitly states that people's values and lifestyles are shown clearly through the clothes they choose to wear. Therefore, clothing reflects personal values and lifestyles, making option B correct. Option A directly contradicts the passage, which identifies clothing as a significant field of human expression. Option C reverses the relationship: clothing is described as sign language, not values as products of sign language. Option D also reverses the meaning by confusing the information communicated through dress with the factors determining clothing choices.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high6268) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:gpt-4o-mini)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>8481eb27a774445923fc...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248351 · SUBLANGENG_Q495730</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_00B285847551 (Question 1 of 1)</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_LANG_ENGLISH — English Language, Reading Comprehension &amp; Verbal Ability</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff hard\">Hard</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: National Standardized English Reading Comprehension Examination (2018-2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: Official Standardized Examination Board · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Aptitude &amp; Comprehension</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Multi-Question Exam Reading Comprehension Passages</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Senior Competitive Exam Comprehension</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Shared Reading Comprehension Passage (high19432)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_00B285847551 · Question 1 of 1</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p>The rain had continued for a week and the flood had created a big river which were running by Nancy Brown&#x27;s farm. As she tried to gather her cows to a higher ground, she slipped and hit her head on a fallen tree trunk. The fall made her unconscious for a moment or two. When she came to, Lizzie, one of her oldest and favorite cows, was licking her face.</p><p>At that time, the water level on the farm was still rising. Nancy gathered all her strength to get up and began walking slowly with Lizzie. The rain had become much heavier, and the water in the field was now waist high. Nancy&#x27;s pace got slower and slower because she felt a great pain in her head. Finally, all she could do was to throw her arm around Lizzie&#x27;s neck and try to hang on. About 20 minutes later, Lizzie managed to pull herself and Nancy out of the rising water and onto a bit of high land, which seemed like a small island in the middle of a lake of white water.</p><p>Even though it was about noon, the sky was so dark and the rain and lightning was so bad that it took rescuers more than two hours to discover Nancy. A man from a helicopter  lowered a rope, but Nancy couldn&#x27;t catch it. A moment later, two men landed on the small island from a ladder in the helicopter. They raised her into the helicopter and took her to the school gym, where the Red Cross had set up an emergency shelter.</p><p>When the flood disappeared two days later, Nancy immediately went back to the &quot;island.&quot; Lizzie was gone. She was one of 19 cows that Nancy had lost in the flood. &quot;I owe my life to her,&quot; said Nancy with tears.</p></div>\n          \n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>What did Nancy try to do before she fell over?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Measure the depth of the river</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Look for a fallen tree trunk</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Protect her cows from being drowned</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">Run away from the flooded farm</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>The passage explicitly states that Nancy was attempting to gather her cows to higher ground when she slipped and struck her head against a fallen tree trunk. This action indicates that she was trying to protect her livestock from the rising floodwaters. Option C correctly expresses her intention. Options A and B introduce actions not mentioned in the passage, while option D incorrectly suggests that she was attempting to escape rather than rescue her cows.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> RACE Official Shared-Passage Exam PYQ (high19432) · AI_AUDITED_VERIFIED (g4f:)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>9c152b88267fd486e3e9...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248350 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489383</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_35EF7857179B (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Required Pump Shaft Input Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 100 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_35EF7857179B · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=75%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 45 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 100 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Using the shared pumping-station data (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math>), determine the mechanical shaft power required from the driving electric motor.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">44.15 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">33.11 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">58.87 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">73.59 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Overall pump efficiency relates useful hydraulic output power to mechanical shaft input power via <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>44.15</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>44.15</mn><mn>0.75</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>58.87</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option B is the classic student trap of multiplying instead of dividing by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>7869b62975a8147ccc4d...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248349 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489382</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_35EF7857179B (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Useful Water (Hydraulic) Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 100 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_35EF7857179B · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=75%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 45 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 100 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Referring to the same pumping station passage, what is the useful hydraulic (water) power imparted to the fluid by the pump?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">4.5 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">44.15 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">58.87 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">33.11 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Useful hydraulic power delivered directly to the water stream depends purely on specific weight, discharge, and manometric head: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>9.81</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>45</mn><mtext> W</mtext></mrow></math> = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>44.15</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option C represents shaft input power, whereas Option D wrongly multiplies hydraulic power by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>0d5fd1e5ddbd32630774...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248348 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489381</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_35EF7857179B (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff easy\">Easy</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Mean Pipe Flow Velocity</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 100 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_35EF7857179B · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=75%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 45 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 100 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Based on the shared pumping-station data above, what is the average flow velocity of water inside the 200 mm delivery pipe?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">3.18 m/s</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0.8 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">6.36 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">4.33 m/s</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Converting volumetric flow rate to SI units gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup><mtext>/s</mtext></mrow></math>. For pipe internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math> (radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>), cross-sectional area is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.031416</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. By the continuity equation, mean velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.18</mn><mtext> m/s</mtext></mrow></math>. Distractor B arises if diameter is mistakenly squared without dividing by 4.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>3eafe82f76b7f32032b8...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248347 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489380</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_69D96C517A4A (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Required Pump Shaft Input Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 80 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_69D96C517A4A · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=70%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 35 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 80 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Using the shared pumping-station data (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math>), determine the mechanical shaft power required from the driving electric motor.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">27.47 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">19.23 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">39.24 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">49.05 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Overall pump efficiency relates useful hydraulic output power to mechanical shaft input power via <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>27.47</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.70</mn></mrow></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27.47</mn><mn>0.70</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>39.24</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option B is the classic student trap of multiplying instead of dividing by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>1215f44d31d4ce16119f...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248346 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489379</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_69D96C517A4A (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Useful Water (Hydraulic) Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 80 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_69D96C517A4A · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=70%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 35 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 80 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Referring to the same pumping station passage, what is the useful hydraulic (water) power imparted to the fluid by the pump?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">2.8 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">27.47 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">39.24 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">19.23 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Useful hydraulic power delivered directly to the water stream depends purely on specific weight, discharge, and manometric head: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>9.81</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.08</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>35</mn><mtext> W</mtext></mrow></math> = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>27.47</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option C represents shaft input power, whereas Option D wrongly multiplies hydraulic power by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>faa2ae0d32a563c8457b...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248345 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489378</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_69D96C517A4A (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff easy\">Easy</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Mean Pipe Flow Velocity</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 80 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_69D96C517A4A · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=70%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 35 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 80 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Based on the shared pumping-station data above, what is the average flow velocity of water inside the 200 mm delivery pipe?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">2.55 m/s</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0.64 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">5.1 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">3.7 m/s</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Converting volumetric flow rate to SI units gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.08</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup><mtext>/s</mtext></mrow></math>. For pipe internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math> (radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>), cross-sectional area is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.031416</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. By the continuity equation, mean velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.55</mn><mtext> m/s</mtext></mrow></math>. Distractor B arises if diameter is mistakenly squared without dividing by 4.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>9b6de81209b55a0b3f0d...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248344 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489377</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_09D2EF07D5EC (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Required Pump Shaft Input Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 60 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_09D2EF07D5EC · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=80%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 40 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 60 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Using the shared pumping-station data (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math>), determine the mechanical shaft power required from the driving electric motor.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">23.54 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">18.83 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">29.42 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">36.78 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Overall pump efficiency relates useful hydraulic output power to mechanical shaft input power via <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>23.54</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.80</mn></mrow></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>23.54</mn><mn>0.80</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>29.42</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option B is the classic student trap of multiplying instead of dividing by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>6d0e0ed18957b72ba3ea...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248343 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489376</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_09D2EF07D5EC (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Useful Water (Hydraulic) Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 60 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_09D2EF07D5EC · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=80%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 40 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 60 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Referring to the same pumping station passage, what is the useful hydraulic (water) power imparted to the fluid by the pump?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">2.4 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">23.54 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">29.42 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">18.83 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Useful hydraulic power delivered directly to the water stream depends purely on specific weight, discharge, and manometric head: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>9.81</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.06</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>40</mn><mtext> W</mtext></mrow></math> = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>23.54</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option C represents shaft input power, whereas Option D wrongly multiplies hydraulic power by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>e84e765c3e25a795e5fc...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248342 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489375</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_09D2EF07D5EC (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff easy\">Easy</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Mean Pipe Flow Velocity</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 60 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_09D2EF07D5EC · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=80%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 40 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 60 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Based on the shared pumping-station data above, what is the average flow velocity of water inside the 200 mm delivery pipe?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">1.91 m/s</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0.48 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">3.82 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">3.06 m/s</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Converting volumetric flow rate to SI units gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.06</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup><mtext>/s</mtext></mrow></math>. For pipe internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math> (radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>), cross-sectional area is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.031416</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. By the continuity equation, mean velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.91</mn><mtext> m/s</mtext></mrow></math>. Distractor B arises if diameter is mistakenly squared without dividing by 4.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>f00b4f178e9b0712714a...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248341 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489374</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_287554D847C6 (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Required Pump Shaft Input Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 50 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_287554D847C6 · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=75%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 25 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 50 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Using the shared pumping-station data (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math>), determine the mechanical shaft power required from the driving electric motor.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">12.26 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">9.2 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">16.35 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">20.44 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Overall pump efficiency relates useful hydraulic output power to mechanical shaft input power via <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12.26</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12.26</mn><mn>0.75</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>16.35</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option B is the classic student trap of multiplying instead of dividing by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>9bc8fcf26dfba0738673...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248340 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489373</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_287554D847C6 (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Useful Water (Hydraulic) Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 50 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_287554D847C6 · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=75%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 25 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 50 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Referring to the same pumping station passage, what is the useful hydraulic (water) power imparted to the fluid by the pump?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">1.25 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">12.26 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">16.35 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">9.2 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Useful hydraulic power delivered directly to the water stream depends purely on specific weight, discharge, and manometric head: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>9.81</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>25</mn><mtext> W</mtext></mrow></math> = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>12.26</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option C represents shaft input power, whereas Option D wrongly multiplies hydraulic power by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>e585fd7a3358cf50ca01...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248339 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489372</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_287554D847C6 (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff easy\">Easy</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Mean Pipe Flow Velocity</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 50 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_287554D847C6 · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=75%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 25 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 50 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Based on the shared pumping-station data above, what is the average flow velocity of water inside the 200 mm delivery pipe?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">1.59 m/s</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0.4 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">3.18 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">2.74 m/s</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Converting volumetric flow rate to SI units gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup><mtext>/s</mtext></mrow></math>. For pipe internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math> (radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>), cross-sectional area is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.031416</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. By the continuity equation, mean velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.59</mn><mtext> m/s</mtext></mrow></math>. Distractor B arises if diameter is mistakenly squared without dividing by 4.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>8b2cbe4bdeddafb947ff...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248338 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489371</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_C8A6E853FA22 (Question 3 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Required Pump Shaft Input Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 40 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_C8A6E853FA22 · Question 3 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=80%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 30 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 40 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Using the shared pumping-station data (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math>), determine the mechanical shaft power required from the driving electric motor.</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">11.77 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">9.42 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">14.71 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">18.39 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option C)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Overall pump efficiency relates useful hydraulic output power to mechanical shaft input power via <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>11.77</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.80</mn></mrow></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11.77</mn><mn>0.80</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>14.71</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option B is the classic student trap of multiplying instead of dividing by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>7ab711fec70c9e01fa23...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248337 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489370</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_C8A6E853FA22 (Question 2 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff medium\">Medium</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Useful Water (Hydraulic) Power</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 40 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_C8A6E853FA22 · Question 2 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=80%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 30 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 40 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Referring to the same pumping station passage, what is the useful hydraulic (water) power imparted to the fluid by the pump?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">1.2 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">11.77 kW</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">14.71 kW</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">9.42 kW</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option B)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Useful hydraulic power delivered directly to the water stream depends purely on specific weight, discharge, and manometric head: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>9.81</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.04</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>30</mn><mtext> W</mtext></mrow></math> = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>11.77</mn><mtext> kW</mtext></mrow></math>. Option C represents shaft input power, whereas Option D wrongly multiplies hydraulic power by efficiency.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>524632e1e71b5bad4274...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248336 · SUBMEFLUID_Q489369</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-psg\">📖 Passage PSG_C8A6E853FA22 (Question 1 of 3)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_ME_FLUID — Fluid Mechanics &amp; Hydraulic Machines</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff easy\">Easy</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: GATE Mechanical / Civil (Common Data Questions) (2022)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: IIT / IISc · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Engineering</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Hydraulic Machines &amp; Centrifugal Pumps</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Common-Data Set: Mean Pipe Flow Velocity</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n        <div class=\"passage-box\">\n          <div class=\"passage-hdr\">\n            <span>📖 Common Data for Linked Questions (Centrifugal Pumping Station — Q = 40 L/s)</span>\n            <span class=\"passage-tag\">Shared ID: PSG_C8A6E853FA22 · Question 1 of 3</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"passage-body\"><p><strong>Common Data Passage:</strong> A municipal water pumping station uses a centrifugal pump of overall efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mtext>%</mtext></mrow></math> to lift water (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><msup><mtext> kg/m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.81</mn><msup><mtext> m/s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>) at a steady discharge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mtext> L/s</mtext></mrow></math> through a uniform delivery pipe of internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext> mm</mtext></mrow></math> against a total manometric head of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>.</p></div>\n          <div class=\"q-diagram-box\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"115\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sump Tank</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"130\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fde68a\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pump η=80%</text>\n  <line x1=\"254\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"395\" y=\"25\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"437\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H = 30 m</text>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q = 40 L/s, D = 200 mm</text>\n</svg></div>\n        </div>\n        \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>Based on the shared pumping-station data above, what is the average flow velocity of water inside the 200 mm delivery pipe?</p></div>\n      \n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">1.27 m/s</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">0.32 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">2.54 m/s</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">2.42 m/s</div></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option A)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Converting volumetric flow rate to SI units gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.04</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup><mtext>/s</mtext></mrow></math>. For pipe internal diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math> (radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mtext> m</mtext></mrow></math>), cross-sectional area is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.031416</mn><msup><mtext> m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. By the continuity equation, mean velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.27</mn><mtext> m/s</mtext></mrow></math>. Distractor B arises if diameter is mistakenly squared without dividing by 4.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Verified Shared-Passage Set · GATE Common-Data</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>1548f575d25b2f3e0e44...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248335 · SUBSCIPHYS_Q489320</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_SCI_PHYSICS — Physics (Classical Mechanics, Electromagnetism, Quantum, Optics &amp; Solid State)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff easy\">Easy</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: NEET UG / JEE Main Physics (2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: NTA · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Science</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Unit:</strong> Ray Optics &amp; Optical Instruments</span> ·\n          <span><strong>Topic:</strong> Thin Convex Lens Image Formation &amp; Ray Tracing</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"q-stem\"><p>As illustrated in the ray diagram, a real object is placed at distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>300.0</mn><mtext> cm</mtext></mrow></math> in front of a thin converging lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mtext> cm</mtext></mrow></math>. At what distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow></math> behind the optical center is the real image formed?</p></div>\n      <div class=\"q-diagram-box\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 220\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">\n  <rect width=\"500\" height=\"220\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"475\" y2=\"115\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/>\n  <path d=\"M250,35 Q272,115 250,195 Q228,115 250,35 Z\" fill=\"rgba(56,189,248,0.28)\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"110\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"110,55 104,68 116,68\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/>\n  <text x=\"110\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#dc2626\">Object (u = 300.0 cm)</text>\n  <line x1=\"110\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#ea580c\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/>\n  <line x1=\"250\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"415\" y2=\"158\" stroke=\"#ea580c\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/>\n  <line x1=\"110\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"152\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"115\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#0f172a\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"133\" text-anchor=\"middle\">F</text>\n  <circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"115\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#0f172a\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"133\" text-anchor=\"middle\">F (f = +50 cm)</text>\n</svg></div>\n      <div class=\"opts-grid\"><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span><div class=\"opt-text\">+42.86 cm</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span><div class=\"opt-text\">+86.0 cm</div></div><div class=\"opt-item \"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span><div class=\"opt-text\">+250.0 cm</div></div><div class=\"opt-item correct-opt\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">D</span><div class=\"opt-text\">+60.0 cm</div><span class=\"corr-tag\">✓ Correct</span></div></div>\n      <details class=\"expl-box\">\n        <summary>View Explanation & Provenance (Answer: Option D)</summary>\n        <div class=\"expl-body\">\n          <p>Using Cartesian sign convention <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>300.0</mn><mtext> cm</mtext></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mtext> cm</mtext></mrow></math>: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>u</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>300.0</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>, yielding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>60.0</mn><mtext> cm</mtext></mrow></math> behind the converging optical center (real, inverted image on the opposite side; Option A wrongly uses +u instead of -u).</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"hash-row\">\n            <span><strong>Source/License:</strong> Recreated Clean Vector SVG Diagram (100% Copyright-Safe)</span>\n            <span><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>3ebf6fe0052d0c19d180...</code></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </article>\n    \n    <article class=\"q-card\">\n      <div class=\"q-head\">\n        <div class=\"q-badges\">\n          <span class=\"badge b-id\">#248334 · SUBSCIPHYS_Q489319</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq-db\">DB2_PYQ</span>\n          \n          \n          <span class=\"badge b-fig\">🖼️ Figure / Diagram</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-loc\">UNIVERSAL: ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-subj\">SUB_SCI_PHYSICS — Physics (Classical Mechanics, Electromagnetism, Quantum, Optics &amp; Solid State)</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-diff easy\">Easy</span>\n          <span class=\"badge b-pyq\">PYQ: NEET UG / JEE Main Physics (2023)</span><span class=\"badge b-meta\">Body: NTA · ALL_COUNTRIES</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"q-meta\">\n          <span><strong>Domain:</strong> Science</span> ·\n          <span><stron